   "langs": "English, Hindi",
   "pronoun": "Him and His",
   "from": "I come from Kushinagar district and completed my higher education—including an M.A. in English and an MBA in Finance & HR—in Bahraich after my family relocated in search of better educational opportunities. My journey into the development sector has been shaped by a blend of grassroots experience and technical expertise. Between 2017 and 2022, working in the financial sector exposed me to ground-level community realities through extensive fieldwork. In April 2025, I joined DEHAT as an Accountant and progressively grew into my current role as an MIS & Training Officer. Interacting with diverse communities and witnessing their challenges firsthand inspired me to commit full-time to the social and development sector. I am motivated to apply my background in finance, MIS, and training to create measurable, positive change in people’s lives.",
   "does": "At DEHAT, I work as an MIS & Training Officer. In simple words, my main job is to keep all our project details, beneficiary records, and field information accurate, safe, and well-organized. Keeping Honest & Accurate Records: Whenever our team conducts an activity or helps a community member, I collect, check, and systematically enter that information. This helps the organization clearly know who received help and what activities took place. Data & Document Management: I manage our project files by scanning important documents, storing them safely online, and organizing our records so that no important information is ever lost. Supporting the Team with Reporting & Training: I assist our team members with data management and report preparation so everyone has the clear information they need to do their work well. In short, I work behind the scenes to make sure all our records are transparent and well-maintained, ensuring our programs run smoothly and community members receive the support they need without delay.",
